Map TCP as well as UDP on the IPv4 target. Mappings carry their protocol and
every lookup matches it, so a UDP and a TCP mapping on the same external
ip:port never alias (otherwise inbound TCP could be DNATed to the host that
owns the UDP mapping). Which protocols reach the target is decided by the
iptables rules (-p udp / -p tcp). The IPv6 target stays UDP only; 200-hardening
rejects IPv6 rules anyway.

